    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="0818" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/27603: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-01T12:00:00-04:00">February 1,
                        1943—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 2:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Now that the President is back the telegram to Ríos must not be delayed
                    since telegrams from all American Presidents and King of England came almost 2
                    weeks ago, and Hull’s telegram to Fernandez<anchor n="24" xml:id="d760-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0819" n="807" xml:id="pg807"/> and Rockefeller’s<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d760-f2"/> to Ríos, Morales and Fernández cannot be given out before
                    Roosevelt’s to Ríos. The latter understands but the public does not and it is
                    not doing us any good.</p>
                <p>Confidential to the President, Secretary and Under Secretary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
